  "releaseNotes": "v3.240.82:\n\t\t- Fixed: GetResourcesByResourceGroupFullPathAsync re-queried for the group it had just\n\t\t  resolved when recurse was false, using the same Eq on FullPath that the group lookup\n\t\t  deliberately avoids - GetResourceGroupByFullPathAsync falls back to a tree node search\n\t\t  precisely because Eq cannot carry parentheses or whitespace. Besides costing a round trip\n\t\t  per group, Eq can return more than the group asked for, and this branch had no guard\n\t\t  against that: the RemoveAll which trims non-matching groups runs only when recursing. A\n\t\t  non-recursive fetch on a bracketed path could therefore return resources belonging to\n\t\t  groups the caller never named, which is the one thing recurse: false should rule out. The\n\t\t  already-resolved group is now used directly.",
